[{"code":"not_implemented","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":10,"col":16},"end":{"line":10,"col":18}},"title":"NOT IMPLEMENTED YET","message":"A limit of the compiler: this `let` of `view` is a pattern, or a binding that\nsomething besides the markup's holes reads — a statement, a `For`'s row, another\nsuch `let` — and its value may have an effect or throw: `inline` evaluates such\na `let` in every binding function that enters the `view`, which is not once per\npass (`docs/design/browser-inline.md` §8.2; §5, class 1). Bind the value with a\nplain `let` the markup reads, or write the call where the markup reads it, or\nbuild this program with `--platform=browser-tea`."}]
